    "title": "2026 Valspar Championship TV schedule, coverage: Where to watch, tee times for Round 3 at Innisbrook",
    "text": "Getty Images The final event of the PGA Tour's Florida Swing shifts west to the gulf coast for the 2026 Valspar Championship on the always-challenging Copperhead Course at Innisbrook Resort. After two rounds, Sungjae Im sits atop the leaderboard at 9 under with David Lipsky one shot back and both Doug Ghim and Chandler Blanchet two back. Im made his mark on Thursday when he played the back nine in 5 under, which included four birdies and an eagle. He had a more uneven day on Friday where he went out with three bogeys and two birdies on the front nine before rallying for three birdies on the back. Now, it's on Im to hold off a host of challengers at the weekend with most four shots or more off the pace. That includes Matthew Fitzpatrick at 5 under as well as Gary Woodland, Tony Finau and Brooks Koepka at 4 under.Here's how you can watch all of the action in Palm Harbor, Florida this weekend. 2026 Valspar Championship TV scheduleAll times EasternRound 3 - SaturdayRound 3 starts: 7:45 a.m. [Tee times]PGA Tour Live: 7:45 a.m. - 6 p.m. -- PGA Tour LiveEarly TV coverage: 1-3 p.m. on Golf ChannelEarly streaming: 1-3 p.m. on GolfChannel.com Live TV coverage: 3-6 p.m. on NBCLive streaming: 3-6 p.m. on PeacockRadio: 1-6 p.m. -- PGA Tour Radio Round 4 - SundayRound 4 starts: 7:45 a.m. [Tee times]PGA Tour Live: 7:45 a.m. - 6 p.m. -- PGA Tour LiveEarly TV coverage: 1-3 p.m. on Golf ChannelEarly streaming: 1-3 p.m. on GolfChannel.comLive TV coverage: 3-6 p.m. on NBCLive streaming: 3-6 p.m. on Peacock Radio: 1-6 p.m. -- PGA Tour Radio",
